- log_q_gyro: gyroscope white noise PSD, (rad/s)^2/Hz per axis, default -8.32, allowed [-9.32, -7.32]
- log_q_ba: accelerometer bias random walk PSD, (m/s^2)^2/s per axis, default -5.00, allowed [-6.00, -4.00]
- log_q_bg: gyroscope bias random walk PSD, (rad/s)^2/s per axis, default -8.00, allowed [-9.00, -7.00]
- log_r_xy: GPS horizontal position noise variance, m^2 per axis (east, north), default -0.22, allowed [-3.22, 2.78]
- log_r_z: GPS vertical position noise variance, m^2, default 0.30, allowed [-2.70, 3.30]

GPS condition to tune for: all (one setting for the whole drive). Estimated horizontal GPS white noise sigma_h = 0.03 m (2-axis standard deviation; this receiver's normal level: 0.03 m). The estimate sees only the fix-to-fix (white) part of the GPS error, not slowly varying errors.

Score: RMS in metres of the filter's prediction error against each new GPS fix, over 17 window(s) of 30 s in this condition. Lower is better.

